        <h1 class="post-detail__title">Community Foundation Welcomes Finance & Operations Manager as part of transition to Independence</h1>

        <div class="post-detail__featured-image">
          <img src="/assets/images/news/64647.webp" alt="Community Foundation Welcomes Finance & Operations Manager as part of transition to Independence" loading="lazy">
        </div>

        <div class="post-detail__content">
          <p>The Community Foundation of Teton Valley is pleased to announce that&nbsp;Sterling Boin&nbsp;has joined the team as&nbsp;Finance &amp; Operations Manager.</p>

<p>As the Foundation moves toward full independence from the Community Foundation of Jackson Hole, internal operations are expanding to meet the community’s growing needs. Sterling’s skills are essential in developing efficient financial systems and ensuring a seamless transition of services to Teton Valley.</p>

<p>Sterling brings extensive experience from both corporate and mission-driven organizations. Most recently, he served as Finance Manager at Polaris and previously as a Senior Financial Analyst for Crocs and the American Alpine Club. He holds an MBA from the University of Colorado Boulder and a BS in Finance and Marketing from Syracuse University.</p>

<p>A Driggs resident, Sterling is actively involved in the local community, volunteering with Teton County Idaho Search and Rescue, Pierre’s Pedal Project, and the Grand Targhee Ski and Snowboard Foundation.</p>

<p><em>“The Community Foundation of Teton Valley is thrilled to have Sterling’s skills, experience, and passion on the team,”&nbsp;</em>said Executive Director&nbsp;Bonnie Self<strong>.</strong>&nbsp;<em>“As we work toward becoming an independent organization, bringing roles like finance and operations in-house is critical to our mission and to serving the community.”</em></p>

<p>&nbsp;The Community Foundation of Teton Valley is excited to continue to provide a comprehensive range of philanthropic services, including donor-advised funds, agency and endowment funds, scholarships, memorial funds, and legacy giving options.</p>
        </div>

